      "text": "(d) Probationary employees, who are not permanent in another title, may utilize the service of or be referred to the EAP. However, probationary employees who have exhibited impaired job-performance must improve performance to the satisfaction of the employing agency before being granted permanent status. At the discretion of the employing agency, the employee's probationary period may be extended no longer than six months in order to participate in the EAP and improve performance.",
